00:58:22,702 --> 00:58:28,702
Brown, Angela Bassett, Forest Whitaker, and Andy Serkis.

17
01:02:01,621 --> 01:02:07,621
In Black Panther, T'Challa is crowned king of Wakanda following his father's death, but he is challenged by
Killmonger (Jordan), who plans to abandon the country's isolationist policies and begin a global revolution.

18
01:05:40,540 --> 01:05:46,540
Wesley Snipes planned to make a Black Panther film in 1992,
but the project did not come to fruition.

19
01:09:19,459 --> 01:09:25,459
In September 2005, Marvel Studios listed a Black Panther film as one of ten films based
on Marvel characters intended to be distributed by Paramount Pictures.

20
01:12:58,378 --> 01:13:04,378
Mark Bailey was hired to write a script in January 2011.

21
01:16:37,297 --> 01:16:43,297
Black Panther was officially announced in October 2014, and Boseman made his first
appearance as the character in Captain America: Civil War (2016).

22
01:20:16,216 --> 01:20:22,216
Cole and Coogler had joined by then, with additional casting in May.

23
01:23:55,135 --> 01:24:01,135
Black Panther was the first Marvel Studios film with a
Black director and a predominantly Black cast.

24
01:27:34,054 --> 01:27:40,054
Principal photography took place from January to April 2017 at EUE/Screen Gems
Studios in the Atlanta metropolitan area, and in Busan, South Korea.

25
01:31:12,972 --> 01:31:18,972
Black Panther premiered at the Dolby Theatre in Los Angeles on January 29, 2018, and was released
theatrically in the United States on February 16, as part of Phase Three of the MCU.

26
01:34:51,891 --> 01:34:57,891
Critics praised its direction, writing, acting (particularly that of Boseman, Jordan, and Wright),
costume design, production values, and soundtrack, but some criticized the visual effects.

27
01:38:30,810 --> 01:38:36,810
Many critics considered the film to be one of the best in the MCU
and it was noted for its cultural significance.

28
01:42:09,729 --> 01:42:15,729
The National Board of Review and the American Film Institute named
Black Panther one of the top-ten films of 2018.

29
01:45:48,648 --> 01:45:54,648
It grossed over $1.3 billion worldwide and broke numerous box office records, becoming the highest-grossing film directed by a Black
filmmaker, the ninth-highest-grossing film at the time of its release, the third-highest-grossing film in the U.S.

30
01:49:27,567 --> 01:49:33,567
and Canada that year, and the second-highest-grossing film of 2018.

31
01:53:06,486 --> 01:53:12,486
Black Panther was nominated for seven awards at the 91st Academy Awards,
winning three, and received numerous other accolades.

32
01:56:45,405 --> 01:56:51,405
It was the first superhero film to receive a Best Picture
nomination, and the first MCU film to win an Academy Award.

33
02:00:24,324 --> 02:00:30,324
A sequel, Black Panther: Wakanda Forever, was released on November 11, 2022, with Wright taking over
as the lead following Boseman's death in 2020, while a third film is in development.

34
02:04:03,243 --> 02:04:09,243
An animated series, Eyes of Wakanda, was released in August 2025 on Disney+.

